        {
          "id": "c2-l001",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "ninos no Xǒguachi. Vide,"
            },
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": " Fago."
            }
          ],
          "note": "This completes the `Fagoita` definition: boards with which children play at `Xǒguachi` ショウガチ, New Year. `Vide, Fago` cross-refers to the preceding entry."
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l002",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Fagotaye."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Comendo algũa couſa dura, ou"
            }
          ],
          "note": "`Fagotaye` is ハゴタエ, modern 歯ごたえ. The Portuguese describes the sensation in the teeth when chewing something hard or difficult."
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l003",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "ruim de maſtigar, &c. ſentila nos dentes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l004",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "Vt."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": " Fago tayegaiſuru."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l005",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Faguchi."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Buraco feito em barro que eſta junto"
            }
          ],
          "note": "`Faguchi` is ハグチ, modern 羽口: the opening by the fire through which a smith's bellows sends air. The physical definition spans three lines."
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l006",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "do fogo por onde o vento dos folles dos ferrei-"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l007",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "ros ſae."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l008",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Fague."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Vt,"
            },
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": " Fague yama."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Monte eſcalua-"
            }
          ],
          "note": "`Fague` is ハゲ; `Fague yama` is ハゲヤマ, a bare mountain. Portuguese `eſcaluado` is modern `escalvado`, “bald or bare.”"
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-l009",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
